Here is the commit message:
JS: remove the horizontal scroll bar reset in getInstance for
 ObjectSelector

Fixes a bug introduced way back in 9e89fc6c1fc522327b0bea270a024f51ff5b120c
(JS: Reset ObjectSelector horz scroll bar to 0 on window open)
that caused the horizontal scroll bar to jitter while a model is running.

Signed-off-by: Harry King <d.harry.king@gmail.com>

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the horizontal scroll bar being reset to 0 every time the `getInstance` method was called, which occurred frequently during the operation of the model. This constant resetting led to a jittering effect as the scroll bar position was abruptly changed, disrupting the user interface experience.

